---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = 'October 26, 2026';
const host = 'Cloudflare Pages';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How the Auva Studio website collects and uses information.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p class="lede">Auva Studio respects your privacy. This policy explains what information this website collects and how it's used.</p>

      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <p>When you use one of my inquiry forms, I collect what you enter: your name, email, business or organization, phone number if you add one, the service you're interested in, your website, and your message. If you book a call, Calendly collects your name, email, and chosen time. Answers to the free website check stay in your browser unless you choose to send them; if you do, I receive your name, email, website, answers, and score. Answers to the free Google profile check also stay in your browser unless you choose to send them. If you do, I receive your name, email, business, town, answers, and score. The business card page can use your camera to show the card in augmented reality. The camera view stays on your phone and is never recorded or sent to me. I don't ask for payment details on this site.</p>

      <h2>How I use it</h2>
      <p>Only to reply to your inquiry, schedule a conversation, and prepare a proposal if you ask for one. I don't sell or rent your information, and I don't add you to a mailing list without your permission.</p>

      <h2>Who helps me</h2>
      <p>Form messages are delivered to me by Web3Forms, a form-processing service, and call bookings are handled by Calendly. The site is hosted by {host}, which may keep standard server logs such as IP addresses and browser type for security.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>I count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which doesn't use cookies or identify you personally.</p>
      <p>If you arrive by clicking one of my Google ads, the site also loads Google's ad tag. It uses cookies so Google can tell me whether an ad led to a message or a booked call, and Google handles that data under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>. Visitors who don't come from an ad don't get this tag. You can opt out of personalized ads anytime in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's ad settings</a>.</p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>I keep inquiry emails as long as needed to respond and for normal business records. Ask me anytime to delete your information.</p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>To see, correct, or delete the information you've sent me, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, I'll update the date above.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>{site.name}, {site.location}<br /><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
